{"ugra": [{"id": "ugra", "headword": "उग्र", "headword_slp1": "ugra", "fold": "ugra", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "उग्र॑ mfn. (said to be fr. √ उच् [Uṇ. ii, 29], but probably fr. a √ उज्, or √ वज्, fr. which also ओजस्, वाज, वज्र may be derived; compar. उग्रतर and ओ॑जीयस्; superl. उग्रतम and ओ॑जिष्ठ), powerful, violent, mighty, impetuous, strong, huge, formidable, terrible", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "high, noble", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "cruel, fierce, ferocious, savage", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "angry, passionate, wrathful", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "hot, sharp, pungent, acrid, RV.; AV.; TS.; R.; Śak.; Ragh. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "उग्र॑ m. N. of Rudra or Śiva, MBh.; VP.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "of a particular Rudra, BhP.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "N. of a mixed tribe (from a Kṣatriya father and Śūdra mother; the Ugra, according to Manu. x, 9, is of cruel or rude [क्रूर] conduct [आचार] and employment [विहार], as killing or catching snakes &c.; but according to the Tantras he is an encomiast or bard), Mn.; Yājñ. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a twice-born man who perpetrates dreadful deeds Comm. on Āp. i, 7, 20; Āp.; Gaut.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "the tree Hyperanthera Moringa, L.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "N. of a Dānava, Hariv.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a son of Dhṛtarāṣṭra, MBh.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "the Guru of Narendrāditya (who built a temple called Ugreśa)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a group of asterisms (viz. पूर्व-फाल्गुनी, पूर्वाषाढा, पूर्व-भाद्रपदा, मघा, भरणी)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "N. of the Malabar country", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "उग्र॑ (अम्), n. a particular poison, the root of Aconitum Ferox", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "wrath, anger;", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "उग्र, [cf. Zd. ughra: Gk. ὑγι-ής, ὑγίεια, Lat.